  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `src/execution_coverage/progress.rs#mod[tests]/impl[RecordingTerm/indicatif::TermLike]/fn[move_cursor_down]` meets the built-in's criteria.\n\n- **Placement and form:** It is a fenced `cite` on an explicit function with a body, which is an allowed target. The explanation is in fenced citation commentary, so it counts as tracked justification.\n- **Substantive reason:** It says why the item is never executed. `TermLike` requires the callback, but the displays are fixed-width and single-line, so nothing moves down. The function is a no-op (`Ok(())`) with no application logic. That is a real reason, not just difficulty.\n- **Agreement with the source:**\n  - `mod[tests]` is marked `#[cfg(test)]`, so the adapter is compiled only for unit tests.\n  - `RecordingTerm`'s `width` returns a fixed 100.\n  - In `impl[Progress]/fn[with_target]`, both progress templates are single-line (`{spinner} {msg} [{elapsed_precise}]`, optionally with a bar and a count). Nothing in them needs a downward cursor move.\n  - The PTY integration test exists as `tests/execution_coverage.rs#fn[coverage_progress_on_a_pty_preserves_reports_and_plain_output_policy]`. It uses `openpty`, so it does exercise real terminal drawing.\n- **Scope:** The exception excuses only this function's zero execution. It does not claim to excuse the file threshold.\n\nI found no gap.",
